  "Main topic of the publication": "This paper investigates the role of myeloid decidual dendritic cells (dDCs) in pregnancy immunoregulation by examining their response to bacterial ligands and bacteria with placenta tropism. The study reveals that dDCs from at-term placentas exhibit a unique gene program and are unable to mature in response to bacterial stimuli, suggesting their involvement in feto-maternal tolerance and susceptibility to intracellular bacteria.",
